cp/mv cp (GNU coreutils) 9.7
=== cp regular-file source ===
--- cp --strip-trailing-slashes w/file.txt/ w/out1 -> rc=1
    stderr: cp: cannot stat 'w/file.txt/': Not a directory
    out1 MISSING
--- cp (no flag)              w/file.txt/ w/out2 -> rc=1
    stderr: cp: cannot stat 'w/file.txt/': Not a directory
--- cp --strip-trailing-slashes w/file.txt  w/out3 (no slash sanity) -> rc=0
    out3 created
=== cp directory source (-r) ===
--- cp -r --strip-trailing-slashes w/dir/ w/dc1 -> rc=0
    dc1 created
--- cp -r (no flag)              w/dir/ w/dc2 -> rc=0
    dc2 created
=== mv parallel (regular-file source) ===
--- mv --strip-trailing-slashes w/file.txt/ w/moved -> rc=1
    stderr: mv: cannot move 'w/file.txt' to 'w/moved': Not a directory
    moved MISSING
